      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/04/british-healthcare-worker-ebola-evacuated-drc-to-uk-document-shows</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Patient is ⁠in ​stable condition and will be transferred to a specialist ‘high consequence’ infectious disease unit&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A British healthcare worker with Ebola is being evacuated from the Democratic Republic of the Congo to the UK for medical treatment, it has been confirmed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;“A British citizen currently in the DR Congo has tested positive for Ebola,” a spokesperson for the UK government said in a statement on Wednesday. “The UK has well-established procedures for dealing with cases like this, and those processes have been activated … The risk to the UK public from Ebola remains low.”&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/04/british-healthcare-worker-ebola-evacuated-drc-to-uk-document-shows"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
