      <title>Flávio Bolsonaro battles to remain relevant as he speaks at rightwing conference at Mar-a-Lago</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/06/flavio-bolsonaro-upbeat-brazil-election-us</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Far-right politician addresses Conservative Political Action Conference and makes unsubstantiated claims about election fraud&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Flávio Bolsonaro, the far-right politician who lost Brazil’s presidential election last month, has insisted his defeat is not “the end for Brazil” as he battles to maintain political relevance after fleeing to the US.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bolsonaro &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/27/flavio-bolsonaro-brazil-argentina-fled"&gt;absconded early last week&lt;/a&gt; shortly after losing the 25 October election to the leftwing incumbent Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva by more than 4m votes.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/06/flavio-bolsonaro-upbeat-brazil-election-us"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
